From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] MIPS: dts: ingenic: t41: wire up the I2C buses

The I2C nodes use the vendor "ingenic,t41-i2c" compatible and carry no
clock, so the mainline jz4780 driver never binds and /dev/i2c-0 never
appears. The sensor helpers (and the GC8613) then have no bus.

Match the T31/X1000 block the driver knows and attach the CGU gates.
The marmot leaf already sets the pinctrl, clock frequency and per-bus
status.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/arch/mips/boot/dts/ingenic/t41.dtsi
+++ b/arch/mips/boot/dts/ingenic/t41.dtsi
@@ -337,30 +337,36 @@
 		};
 
 		i2c0: i2c@0x10050000 {
-			compatible = "ingenic,t41-i2c";
+			compatible = "ingenic,t41-i2c", "ingenic,t31-i2c";
 			reg = <0x10050000 0x1000>;
 			interrupt-parent = <&core_intc>;
 			interrupts = <IRQ_I2C0>;
+			clocks = <&clock T41_CLK_I2C0>;
+			clock-names = "i2c";
 			#address-cells = <1>;
 			#size-cells = <0>;
 			status = "okay";
 		};
 
 		i2c1: i2c@0x10051000 {
-			compatible = "ingenic,t41-i2c";
+			compatible = "ingenic,t41-i2c", "ingenic,t31-i2c";
 			reg = <0x10051000 0x1000>;
 			interrupt-parent = <&core_intc>;
 			interrupts = <IRQ_I2C1>;
+			clocks = <&clock T41_CLK_I2C1>;
+			clock-names = "i2c";
 			#address-cells = <1>;
 			#size-cells = <0>;
 			status = "okay";
 		};
 
 		i2c2: i2c@0x10052000 {
-			compatible = "ingenic,t41-i2c";
+			compatible = "ingenic,t41-i2c", "ingenic,t31-i2c";
 			reg = <0x10052000 0x1000>;
 			interrupt-parent = <&core_intc>;
 			interrupts = <IRQ_I2C2>;
+			clocks = <&clock T41_CLK_I2C2>;
+			clock-names = "i2c";
 			#address-cells = <1>;
 			#size-cells = <0>;
 			status = "okay";
